{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/archive/component/aspace_38cd90e8743f479e6b8bfc6f83f17265","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"aspace_38cd90e8743f479e6b8bfc6f83f17265","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Maria Chabot to Mabel Ludlum","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"abstract","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/abstract"}],"content":"MABEL STEWART LUDLUM [a.k.a.: \"Sister Mabel\"; Mrs. Seymour DeWitt Ludlum] Correspondence from Maria Chabot to Mabel Ludlum: Five letters and five postcards, Dec. 20, 1937 - Sept. 24, [1944]. Chabot's letter of Sept. 24, [1944] is a response to Ludlum's letter of Sept. 17, 1944. There is a photocopy of Chabot's letter of Dec. 1941 to Ludlum in this binder. Correspondence from Mabel Ludlum to Maria Chabot: Six letters and one envelope without contents, Oct. 28, 1933 - Sept. 17, 1944. The envelope without contents has, however, a recipe on the front and a pencil note on the back. There is a photocopy of Ludlum's letter of Jan. 6, 1941 in this binder.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Related Material","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/relatedmaterial"}],"content":[],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Legal status statement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/userestrict"}],"content":null,"type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}